.Dd November 5, 2026
.Dt TEE 1
.Os ABSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm tee
.Nd copy standard input to standard output and files
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl ai
.Op Ar file ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Read standard input until end of input and copy it to standard output and
each named file.
Without file operands, copy only to standard output.
Files are created or truncated by default.
.Fl a
appends instead of truncating.
.Pp
If one file cannot be opened or an output fails, report the error and
continue copying to the other outputs.
The final status is nonzero when any output failed.
Input and output are byte streams; no newline conversion is performed.
.Sh UNSUPPORTED ON ABSD
This is the unmodified sbase 0.1 implementation from the pinned archive;
see
.Xr sbase 7 .
.Fl i
is recognized but refused before any file is opened: ABSD's existing
signal adapter returns ENOSYS for signal dispositions, including SIG_IGN.
The error is reported on standard error with a nonzero status.
.Pp
File access uses the process's inherited filesystem view.
Unix owners, permission bits and signal delivery are not provided.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when input was copied without error, nonzero on invalid options,
input/output errors or the unsupported signal option.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
cd /home/operator
/bin/echo "keep this" | tee notes.txt
/bin/echo "more" | tee -a notes.txt
cat notes.txt
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cat 1 ,
.Xr filesystem 7 ,
.Xr sbase 7
